## Errors & Mistakes
The first implementation did not trim spaces after !=. The user hit it on real data: planner get --repo "!= coreweave/inference-tools" listed every coreweave/inference-tools plan and exited 0, because the filter text was " coreweave/inference-tools" with a leading space. The first round of tests used only tight spellings, so they missed it. In the first test pass, TestRepoFilterRejectsBareExclusion failed with "plan root does not exist" because validation had not been added yet; that was the expected red state. I briefly drafted a completion case for typing a lone "!" and removed it before running, since completion only adds the prefix once "!=" is typed.

## Dead Ends
Trimming inside matchesRepo was not used. It would run once per plan and leave the bare "!= " check in a different place from the bare "!=" check. Normalizing once in validate keeps both checks together and keeps matchesRepo a pure comparison. A general selector parser (=, ==, comma lists) was out of scope per the plan.

## Hints for Future Agents
listOptions.validate runs before resolveRoot, so tests for flag validation can point --root at a missing directory and still expect the validation error. validate mutates o.repo (it stores "!=" plus the trimmed text), which is how matchesRepo sees a clean filter. Only spaces after != are trimmed; a positive --repo value is still used verbatim, as before. The tree intentionally shows an excluded ancestor (widgets-umbrella under --repo '!=widgets') when an included child (gadgets-cross-child) needs it, through markVisible. Use git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null for commits and merges here, because the post-commit hook on master pushes to origin.

## Codebase Discoveries
matchesRepo is the single point for --repo semantics: selects, hidden, and inactive in tree.go all call it, so the "No plans found" and hidden-plan notes follow the filter automatically. Repository completion goes through completer.repos and completeValues, which does a plain prefix match, so a prefixed label list is enough for != completion. The fixture corpus in testdata/plans has acme/widgets, acme/gadgets, acme/gizmos, and a loose plan with no repository; get hides 4 plans without valid front matter by default and tree hides 3, because the tree shows the legacy parent of an active child.

